    "Devengado" : {
      "localizations" : {
        "en" : {
          "stringUnit" : {
            "state" : "translated",
            "value" : "Accrual"
          }
        }
      }
    },
    "Devengado: la venta cuenta al facturarla y el gasto al recibir la factura, aunque aún no se cobre ni se pague. Caja: solo cuenta lo que ya entró o salió del banco. Muchos negocios pequeños declaran en caja; pregúntale a tu contador cuál usas." : {
      "localizations" : {
        "en" : {
          "stringUnit" : {
            "state" : "translated",
            "value" : "Accrual: a sale counts when you invoice it and an expense when you receive the bill, even if it isn't collected or paid yet. Cash: only what already came in or went out of the bank counts. Many small businesses file on a cash basis; ask your accountant which one you use."
          }
        }
      }
    },
